//! std/prelude: the two enums that `try` and `expr else d` are syntax over.
//! They are in scope in every program without an import. Nothing else lives here (no externs, no
//! helpers, no allocation), so it is safe to inject everywhere. Helper fns (mget, vget, lookup_or,
//! …) stay in std/result behind an explicit import.

/// `Result<T, E>` is the full form; the error type may be omitted: `Result<T>` is `Result<T, Str>`
/// (the compiler normalizes the shorthand, so an `Err` payload is always typed).
pub enum Option<T> { Some(T) None }
pub enum Result<T, E> { Ok(T) Err(E) }
